# ⚠️ .easignore REPLACES .gitignore for EAS Build uploads — it does not add to it.
# https://docs.expo.dev/build-reference/easignore/
#
# So every pattern from .gitignore has to be repeated here. This file previously
# listed only the big reference folders, which meant the two lines that matter
# most — /ios and /android — were NOT excluded. EAS therefore uploaded the stale
# local prebuild (generated 2026-07-17) and built from it instead of regenerating
# from app.json (last changed 2026-07-27).
#
# Consequence, before this fix: production builds shipped WITHOUT
# NSCameraUsageDescription / NSPhotoLibraryUsageDescription and without
# ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption — an App Review rejection, plus a hard crash the
# moment a user tapped to pick a photo.
#
# If you edit this file, keep the .gitignore section below in sync.

# ── mirrored from .gitignore ────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/

.expo/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts

.kotlin/
*.orig.*
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision

.metro-health-check*

npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*

.DS_Store
*.pem

.env*.local

*.tsbuildinfo

# Generated native folders. EAS regenerates these from app.json (Continuous
# Native Generation). Uploading them makes the build "bare" and freezes whatever
# config was in place when they were last generated locally.
/ios
/android

play-service-account.json

# ── EAS-specific: keep ~1 GB of reference material out of every upload ──────
EyeScout app/
SaaS app /
Untitled*.pdf

# Large videos, named individually rather than with a blanket *.mp4.
#
# A blanket *.mp4 also excluded assets/intro.mp4 — which IntroVideo.tsx pulls in
# with require('../../assets/intro.mp4'). Metro resolves that require at bundle
# time on the EAS builder, so excluding it fails the build outright.
intro-original.mp4
hf_*.mp4
